/target
/samples/*
!/samples/contrast/
# The projects part's finished programs (bs10). Tracked, because a reader
# can take the whole file and because `cargo xtask verify-docs` measures
# them: each must appear verbatim in the chapter that prints it, and the
# chapter's `wc` claims are recomputed against them. Everything else
# under samples/ is generated (extracted, export, selftest).
!/samples/projects/
# The ecosystem part's package fixtures (bs09). Tracked, because the
# chapters quote these files byte for byte (a fence carrying
# `file(path)`) and replay commands inside copies of these trees (a
# `console,in(pkg/name)` block), so a fixture is as much a part of the
# book as a paragraph. Manifests, ledgers and programs all belong here.
!/samples/pkg/
# Compiler-side build caches, wherever a `wolf build` was run.
.lu-cache/
